# Tutorial: Channel `agent`

This tutorial describes the channel `agent`. To read it again later, use the `clawp_read_tutorial` tool with topic `channel_agent`.

The `agent` channel is used by agents within the Clawp framework to communicate within the system.

## Incoming channel descriptor

The channel descriptor on incoming messages has these keys:

- `type`: Always the literal `agent`.
- `sender_id`: (string representing a UUID) Agent ID of the sender.

Example channel metadata for incoming messages:

```
{{
  "type": "matrix",
  "sender_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}}
```

## Outgoing channel descriptor

For outgoing messages (when you send), you only need to specify `type` and `recipient_id` (the agent's ID as a UUID string).

Example channel header for outgoing messages:

```
{{"type":"agent","recipient_id":"11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"}}
```
